      "score": 23,
      "comments": 7,
      "author": "signal-11",
      "published": "2026-10-28T09:47:41Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Achieving billion-query-per-second throughput requires flat, compact memory layouts that eliminate pointer indirection and fit within L1/L2 CPU caches.",
        "SIMD instructions like AVX2 and AVX-512 enable branchless batch processing, evaluating multiple lookup keys per clock cycle.",
        "Minimal perfect hashing and explicit hardware prefetching minimize latency and cache misses, enabling linear multi-core scaling without lock contention."
      ]
    },
